    "created_at": "2019-09-02T21:29:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-02T21:29:26Z",
    "body": "These are good questions. Some events are fired and some are not, and the criteria isn't obvious.\r\n\r\nFor the \"seeked\" event, I expect that's not fired because it wouldn't be quite true, the seek is aborted and never finished, but there is no \"seekabort\" event. In other cases where \"seeked\" is fired, one has successfully reached the requested playback position.\r\n\r\nWhy \"timeupdate\" can be fired but \"durationchange\" not is harder to understand. Sure, `video.duration` will be NaN, but that's the initial value just like 0 is for `video.currentTime`. I suppose the omission isn't very serious because if the resource selection algorithm picks a new source, then a \"durationchange\" event will soon be fired with the new duration.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
